# Ironworks Setup & Understand (L1–L2)

## L1 — /iron:init — Project Bootstrap

Scaffold from zero to production-ready.

### Stack Detection

Detects 16+ stacks: Next.js, React, Vue, Angular, SvelteKit, Express, FastAPI, Django, Laravel, Go, Rust, Java/Spring, Scala, Elixir/Phoenix, .NET, Flutter.

### Scaffolded Files

- `CLAUDE.md` — project instructions for AI agents
- `CONTEXT.md` — domain vocabulary and shared terms
- `.env.example` — environment variable template
- `ironworks/specs/` — spec storage directory
- `docs/adr/` — architecture decision records
- CI config (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc.)
- `git init` with `.gitignore`

### Variants

- `--stack <name>` — skip auto-detection, use specified stack
- `--minimal` — git + CLAUDE.md + .gitignore only

### Rules

- Never overwrite existing files
- No placeholder code — every generated file must be functional
- Scaffold must pass its own CI on first run

